{"title":"2002 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 4","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>An integer is divided by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0a0db32027a732ac57d37ef2ae9bb150f65b108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and the remainder is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. An example of such an integer is\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/f/d0f38fa8a023e378e4d280b6bf46fe258bfc400e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{ (A) }\\ 14 \\qquad\\text{ (B) }\\ 15 \\qquad\\text{ (C) }\\ 16 \\qquad\\text{ (D) }\\ 17 \\qquad\\text{ (E) }\\ 18$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"433\" height=\"18\" />  \n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>From the first sentence, we know that the integer must be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> more than a multiple of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0a0db32027a732ac57d37ef2ae9bb150f65b108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> since we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/3/8438343dcb5f6c95edab583a2c7996a9966bb9b3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7q + 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"51\" height=\"17\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/1/0615acc3725de21025457e7d6f7694dab8e2f758.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> is an integer.\n</p><p>Looking at the answer choices, we see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/2/6/b26ba7a6ccc7381991d744491ce8fa1760f6e77a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed {\\textbf {(E) } 18}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"65\" height=\"30\" /> is the only one that satisfies this requirement.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)\" title=\"2002 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8)\">2002 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8)</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2002 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems (page does not exist)\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Answer_Key&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2002 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Answer Key (page does not exist)\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cemc.math.uwaterloo.ca/contests/past_contests.html\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2002 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 3\">Problem 3</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /